    <notes>

        T10Link: Honeywell Home T9 / T10 / T10 Pro thermostats controlled LOCALLY (Apple HomeKit protocol on the LAN),
        through the T10Link bridge service. No Honeywell/Resideo cloud and no Resideo account are needed.
        Full manual: the Documentation tab.

        A BRIDGE IS REQUIRED
        This profile talks to the T10Link bridge, a small service that is paired with the thermostat over HomeKit.
        It runs on the Savant host Mac itself, another Mac, a Raspberry Pi or any Linux box on the same network.
        If the bridge is NOT on the Savant host, add the Savant host's IP to allowed_clients in the bridge's
        config.json, or the bridge refuses Savant's connection.

        SETUP
        1. Install the bridge and pair it once:  t10link pair  (Menu > Connect HomeKit on the thermostat shows the
           code; it changes each time that screen opens). The thermostat must not already be in Apple Home.
        2. Ethernet: set Device IP Address to the machine running the bridge. Port 2400.
        3. HVAC data table: one row. Controller = this component, Entity = Zone, ThermostatAddress [1] = 1.
           Tick Heat, Cool and Auto as the system supports. Leave Fan unticked: HomeKit doesn't expose fan mode.
        4. Upload the configuration.

        WHAT WORKS (T10 firmware 1.5.3)
          Mode Off/Heat/Cool/Auto, heat and cool setpoints, current temperature, humidity, heating/cooling
          state, RedLINK room sensors (temperature, humidity, motion), occupancy, filter reminders.
          Fan mode and hold are not available over HomeKit.

        SAVANT SCHEDULER
          Turn the thermostat's own schedule OFF (at the thermostat) and let Savant's climate scheduler run it.
          The T10 only takes the setpoint of the mode it's in (Heat: heat setpoint, Cool: cool setpoint, Auto: both).
          A setpoint for the other mode is saved by the bridge (T_SAVED_SETPOINTS), shown in Savant, and written
          as soon as the thermostat switches to that mode.

        STATES
          Savant HVAC: ThermostatCurrentTemperature_1, ThermostatCurrentHeatPoint_1, ThermostatCurrentCoolPoint_1,
          ThermostatCurrentHumidity_1, ThermostatMode_1, IsCurrentHVACMode*_1, IsCurrentHVACState*_1.
          T_MODE, T_STATE, T_TEMP, T_HEAT_SETPOINT, T_COOL_SETPOINT, T_PENDING, T_ERROR, T_FILTER1_CHANGE ...
          SENSORn_NAME / _TEMP / _HUMIDITY / _MOTION for up to 4 room sensors.
          SYS_ONLINE (gate automations on 1), SYS_ERROR, SYS_PAIRED. Full list in STATES.md / the Documentation tab.

        Thermostat state is only ever set from what the thermostat reports, never assumed from a button press.

        ====================== Change Log ==================
        Version: 1.2.0 Change: The bridge now installs on macOS (including the Savant host) as well as Linux / Raspberry Pi (32- and 64-bit). Profile unchanged apart from these notes.
        Version: 1.1.2 Change: Auto can now be ticked in the HVAC data table. Blueprint enables the Auto column only when the profile has the ThermostatCurrentSetPoint state, so the bridge now sends ThermostatCurrentSetPoint_1 (the active setpoint in Heat / Cool). Needs bridge 1.1.2.
        Version: 1.1.1 Change: HVAC section matches Savant's own Honeywell T-Series profile for Auto (dual setpoint): added IncreaseTemperatureAuto / DecreaseTemperatureAuto and the CurrentAutoChangeOverStatus state variable (CurrentChangeOverStatus_1, true in Auto).
        Version: 1.1.0 Change: Works with Savant's climate scheduler: a setpoint for the mode the thermostat isn't in is saved and applied when it switches mode, instead of being refused. New T_SAVED_SETPOINTS state and ClearSavedSetpoints action.
        Version: 1.0.0 Change: First release. Savant connection on port 2400.

    </notes>
